    "done_when": "reckon/mcp.py _discovery_summary and the roadmap summary view (reckon/mcp_views.py or reckon/roadmap.py) both carry a sprints list, computed once in Python and shared by both. Each row gives the sprint id, theme, stored status, the section 2 liveness fields, member and pending counts, completion percentage, and closed_at for a closed sprint. sprint_recent_days defaults to 14 and is read from flight config. A new tests/test_summaries_list_live_and_recent_sprints.py builds a synthetic project under a temporary config home with one live, one open idle, one closed 3 days ago and one closed 40 days ago, with dates derived from a fixture clock, not literals. It asserts the first three appear in that order in both summaries and the fourth does not. A case asserts the reckon project's discovery summary at the worktree head stays under the response budget, recording its measured length. The declared mutation, dropping the recent-closed window, fails the ordering case. The sprint, roadmap and mcp summary test files show zero added failures by id against the dispatch base, run with the absolute venv python and a neutral basetemp on node-local /tmp. baseline_suite and after_suite are one-line JSON with revision, tree, full command, exit_status, absolute log_path, completed, failure_count and failure_ids, negative_control_log is a top-level absolute path whose log ends in EXIT=, and a tests: field is recorded",
